  "caveats": [
    "IC50_*_value is the numeric bound for censored rows, so any code that reads it directly (including the paper-funnel binary label) treats '>100 uM' as exactly 100 uM. This table keeps the censoring flag so the two can be separated.",
    "Censoring is not random: 18.4% of paper-funnel Ru rows are right-censored vs 10.7% for Re. Dropping censored rows biases every metal median toward potent compounds, and biases metals unequally. Report both the exact-only and the bound-imputed view.",
    "Matched cross-metal units are a small, non-random subset of each metal's cohort (see matched_pairs). They are the only units that identify a substitution effect without a between-paper confound, so every Delta must carry its n.",
    "Phototoxicity needs dark and light IC50 on the same source row; the source does not pair measurements across rows, so a paper that reports light/dark in separate rows contributes no PI.",
    "SMILES_Ligands is a mixture string that may embed counterions; n_fragments records the fragment count but ligand identity is the whole canonical string, matching the classification mainline so cohorts stay comparable.",
    "Cell-line keys merge 16 spelling variants and keep the p53 +/- pair apart. Keys are declared, not inferred from ontology lookup."
  ]
